{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OISF/suricata/compare/main...6d437956e2ed2da75976d7635cbe09a953d3c489","html_url":"https://github.com/OISF/suricata/compare/main...6d437956e2ed2da75976d7635cbe09a953d3c489","permalink_url":"https://github.com/OISF/suricata/compare/OISF:c48ca37...OISF:6d43795","diff_url":"https://github.com/OISF/suricata/compare/main...6d437956e2ed2da75976d7635cbe09a953d3c489.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/OISF/suricata/compare/main...6d437956e2ed2da75976d7635cbe09a953d3c489.patch","base_commit":{"sha":"c48ca372deb3befae42f3dbcaa75467e20dbae3b","node_id":"C_kwDOAFKNutoAKGM0OGNhMzcyZGViM2JlZmFlNDJmM2RiY2FhNzU0NjdlMjBkYmFlM2I","commit":{"author":{"name":"Victor Julien","email":"vjulien@oisf.net","date":"2026-11-11T11:07:48Z"},"committer":{"name":"Victor Julien","email":"vjulien@oisf.net","date":"2026-11-11T22:05:10Z"},"message":"rust: update rustix to 1.1.6\n\nThe xattr helpers mark as many bytes initialized as the syscall reported, but\na zero-length buffer is a size query: nothing is written and the reported size\nis the attribute or name-list size. A Vec whose length equals its capacity\nreaches that from safe code, and rustix then set the length past the capacity\nover memory that was never written.\n\nrustyline gets rustix through fd-lock, so suricatasc carries it.\n\nLock file only: 1.1.6 declares the same dependency set as the version it\nreplaces, so nothing else moves.\n\nhttps://rustsec.org/advisories/RUSTSEC-2026-0486","tree":{"sha":"236d06b727d2e14820ac9b5d16bc5d236a2aaa58","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OISF/suricata/git/trees/236d06b727d2e14820ac9b5d16bc5d236a2aaa58"},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OISF/suricata/git/commits/c48ca372deb3befae42f3dbcaa75467e20dbae3b","comment_count":0,"verification":{"verified":false,"reason":"unsigned","signature":null,"payload":null,"verified_at":null}},"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/OISF/suricata/commits/c48ca372deb3befae42f3dbcaa75467e20dbae3b","html_url":"https://github.com/OIS